<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maeandrius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 522 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maeandrius was the secretary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polycrates">Polycrates</a>, tyrant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a>, and took control of the island after his master's murder around 522 BCE. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> he offered the Samians equal rights but kept power for himself. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otanes">Otanes</a> came to install Polycrates' brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syloson">Syloson</a>, he surrendered and left for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>, while his brother's attack on the Persians brought a massacre of the Samians.</p></div>
